Load Satin's viewer controller and its stylesheet.

This is the only change Satin makes to the pdf.js distribution; every other
file is byte-identical to the official release (pdfjs-6.2.108-dist.zip from
https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js/releases/tag/v6.2.108).

The tags go after viewer.mjs because that module publishes
window.PDFViewerApplication as its body runs, and the controller needs it. The
color engine is not injected here: viewer.js imports it, and opens the document
itself, so nothing is painted before the canvas accessors are in place.

--- a/web/viewer.html
+++ b/web/viewer.html
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 
     <link rel="stylesheet" href="viewer.css" />
 
-  <script src="viewer.mjs" type="module"></script>
+  <script src="viewer.mjs" type="module"></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../tint/viewer.css" /><script src="../../tint/viewer.js" type="module"></script>
   </head>
 
   <body tabindex="0">
